  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guinea Bissau -  Public Administration and Finance Reform Programme (PRAFP),  Phase I</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Guin&#xe9;e Bissau - Programme de r&#xe9;formes de l&apos;administration et des finances publiques (PRAFP), phase I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">La Direction soumet la proposition et la recommandation suivantes pour l&apos;octroi d&apos;un don de la Facilit&#xe9; d&apos;appui &#xe0; la transition (FAT) de 5 millions d&apos;UC &#xe0; la R&#xe9;publique de Guin&#xe9;e-Bissau pour financer la premi&#xe8;re phase du Programme de r&#xe9;forme de l&apos;administration et des finances publiques (PRAFP-I). Le PRAFP-I est la premi&#xe8;re phase d&apos;une op&#xe9;ration d&apos;appui budg&#xe9;taire programmatique couvrant les exercices 2024 et 2025, avec un budget indicatif de 10 millions d&apos;UC.  L&apos;op&#xe9;ration propos&#xe9;e est une r&#xe9;ponse &#xe0; la demande d&apos;assistance financi&#xe8;re du gouvernement sous forme d&apos;appui budg&#xe9;taire pour combler une partie du d&#xe9;ficit de financement pour les exercices 2024 et 2025. La demande a &#xe9;t&#xe9; faite dans un contexte de d&#xe9;clin de l&apos;activit&#xe9; &#xe9;conomique et de d&#xe9;t&#xe9;rioration des finances publiques en raison des effets n&#xe9;fastes de la pand&#xe9;mie de COVID-19 et de multiples chocs. Elle s&apos;inscrit &#xe9;galement dans le cadre des efforts d&apos;assainissement budg&#xe9;taire du gouvernement soutenus par la facilit&#xe9; &#xe9;largie de cr&#xe9;dit (FEC) du FMI. Le projet contribue au financement climatique, avec une enveloppe de 2 millions USD du montant total approuv&#xe9; d&#xe9;di&#xe9;e &#xe0; l&#x2019;att&#xe9;nuation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Management  submits  the following  proposal  and  recommendation  for  the  award  of  a Transition  Support  Facility  (TSF)  grant  of  UA  5  million  to  the  Republic  of  Guinea-Bissau  to finance the first phase of the Public Administration and Finance Reform Programme (PRAFP-I). PRAFP-I is the first phase of a programme-based budget support operation covering the 2024  and  2025  financial  years,  with  an  indicative  budget  of  UA  10  million.  The  proposed operation is a response to the Government&apos;s request for financial assistance in the form of budget support to bridge part of the financing gap for the 2024 and 2025 financial years. The request was made against a backdrop of declining economic activity and deteriorating public finance due to the adverse effects of the COVID-19 pandemic, and multiple shocks. It was also in line with the Government&#x2019;s fiscal consolidation efforts supported by the IMF&apos;s Extended Credit Facility (ECF). The project contributes to climate finance, with 2 million USD of the total approved amount dedicated to mitigation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Le programme b&#xe9;n&#xe9;ficiera directement &#xe0; tous les Bissau-Guin&#xe9;ens, car l&apos;am&#xe9;lioration des r&#xe9;sultats budg&#xe9;taires contribuera &#xe0; r&#xe9;duire les facteurs de vuln&#xe9;rabilit&#xe9; &#xe9;conomique et sociale en am&#xe9;liorant la qualit&#xe9; et l&apos;efficacit&#xe9; des d&#xe9;penses publiques. Le renforcement de la transparence dans la gestion des finances publiques et de l&apos;efficacit&#xe9; budg&#xe9;taire pour augmenter la collecte des recettes int&#xe9;rieures, combin&#xe9; &#xe0; un meilleur contr&#xf4;le des d&#xe9;penses publiques et de la masse salariale, peut cr&#xe9;er une marge de man&#x153;uvre budg&#xe9;taire pour am&#xe9;liorer les services publics et, par cons&#xe9;quent, les conditions de vie de la population. Cette marge de man&#x153;uvre budg&#xe9;taire permettra &#xe9;galement de financer les infrastructures sociales.  Le programme contribuera ainsi &#xe0; renforcer la comp&#xe9;titivit&#xe9; de l&apos;&#xe9;conomie et, partant, l&apos;attractivit&#xe9; du pays.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The  programme  will  directly  benefit  all  Guinea-Bissauans,  as  improved  fiscal performance  will  contribute  to  reducing  economic  and  social  vulnerability  factors  by improving the quality and effectiveness of public spending. Enhanced transparency in public finance management and budgetary efficiency to increase domestic revenue collection, combined with better control of public spending and the wage bill, can create fiscal space to improve public services and, therefore, the living conditions of the people. Such fiscal space will also allow for the  financing  of  social  infrastructure.  In  this  way,  the  programme  will  help  to  strengthen  the competitiveness of the economy and, hence, the country&apos;s attractiveness.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PRAFP is a two-phase programme-based budget support operation with a single fixed tranche  per  phase.  The  programme  development  goal  is  to  support  public  administration  and economic   resilience   by   strengthening   fiscal   sustainability   and   improving   public finance management  control  and  transparency. More  specifically,  the  programme  aims  to:  (i)  support domestic  revenue  collection  and  public  expenditure  control;  and  (ii)  strengthen  public  finance management control and transparency in public procurement. In doing so, it addresses the main challenges and constraints faced by Guinea-Bissau.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The PRAFP is a two-phase programme-based budget support operation with a single fixed tranche  per  phase.  The  programme  development  goal  is  to  support  public  administration  and economic   resilience   by   strengthening   fiscal   sustainability   and   improving   public finance management  control  and  transparency. More  specifically,  the  programme  aims  to:  (i)  support domestic  revenue  collection  and  public  expenditure  control;  and  (ii)  strengthen  public  finance management control and transparency in public procurement. In doing so, it addresses the main challenges and constraints faced by Guinea-Bissau.</narrative>
  </description>
